00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:53.170
And you can already today
open up the demo at this URL.

00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:58.640
All right.

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:03.740
And so the second area
that I want to cover

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:05.780
is developer tools.
So you may have

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:09.200
seen Olga's great talk
about best practices

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:11.900
and just about before.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:16.630
And what she did was, she
showed a lot of best practices

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:21.470
that we use in the community.

00:22:21.470 --> 00:22:24.300
And she did this in a
non opinionated way.

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.350
So that no matter what were
there were some examples,

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:30.260
but no matter what
technology choices you make,

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:32.260
you can still use
these best practices.

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:35.330
There are a lot of
options. At the same time,

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:39.590
at Appsilon we are building
projects and development

00:22:39.590 --> 00:22:45.620
workflow tools that realize
these best practices in a very

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:49.300
opinionated way, which
is, in our opinion,

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:53.330
just works best
for most projects.

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:55.310
So today, I'd like
to share with you

00:22:55.310 --> 00:23:00.440
that we will be publishing,
the first of its kind Shiny

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:02.660
application framework.

00:23:02.660 --> 00:23:06.740
So I think that on
top of Shiny and let you

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:11.930
be more efficient for
building production apps,

00:23:11.930 --> 00:23:16.640
so there are a lot of areas
that you can take care

00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:19.910
of to make your app work
well in production.

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:24.500
You don't necessarily have
to take care of all of them.

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:28.730
Bu if you do,
it really, really

00:23:28.730 --> 00:23:31.640
increases your
chances of success.

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:36.480
So over the years, we've built
tools for all of these areas.

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:40.850
And in the coming months, we
will be gradually sharing them

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:42.811
as a unified framework.

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.850
So why does this matter?

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:52.090
Basically, all of the points
from the previous slide matter,

00:23:52.090 --> 00:23:55.240
because ultimately
for appss that work

00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:59.810
in production, that users,
your users depend on them.

00:23:59.810 --> 00:24:02.770
And we need to ensure
that they're, first

00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:07.030
of all, reliable and easy
to maintain, but also

00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:08.530
for our projects
to be successful,

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:11.380
we need to do that to
achieve maintainability

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:17.170
and reliability while keeping
the development velocity high,

00:24:17.170 --> 00:24:23.420
which like keep the philosophy
that Shiny is famous for.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:25.480
So just some
examples of what you

00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:28.400
will get with the
framework out of the box,

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:32.450
much richer domain driven
application structure

00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:35.440
and tests.

00:24:35.440 --> 00:24:39.330
Like on this example of cypress.

00:24:39.330 --> 00:24:42.720
Comprehensive but easy to
use dependency management

00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:46.390
like Olga mentioned.

00:24:46.390 --> 00:24:49.800
Data validation.

00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:54.440
So what's really new here
compared to existing solutions?

00:24:54.440 --> 00:24:56.530
I think there are
three main things.

00:24:56.530 --> 00:24:59.250
First of all, it's a
complete framework,

00:24:59.250 --> 00:25:01.890
a complete ecosystem covering.

00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:06.870
Giving you an option
for all of the points

00:25:06.870 --> 00:25:08.290
that you need to think of.

00:25:08.290 --> 00:25:12.980
And then it's just,

00:25:12.980 --> 00:25:14.930
the fact that we
bring best practices

00:25:14.930 --> 00:25:17.990
from other
technologies and areas

00:25:17.990 --> 00:25:20.870
where we're as the
Shiny community, we

00:25:20.870 --> 00:25:25.490
can benefit most by learning
from other technologies

00:25:25.490 --> 00:25:28.810
and the third.

00:25:28.810 --> 00:25:33.040
You get all these
best practices, not as

00:25:33.040 --> 00:25:37.060
knowledge, but as code, so
you can start your project

00:25:37.060 --> 00:25:39.310
from scratch with all the
best practices included

00:25:39.310 --> 00:25:43.840
and you can learn watching,
which parts you need,

00:25:43.840 --> 00:25:45.730
like you can learn
each part that you

00:25:45.730 --> 00:25:49.280
need from the code that is
already in your project.

00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:51.730
And it's already working.

00:25:51.730 --> 00:25:55.390
And you can learn from that.

00:25:55.390 --> 00:26:00.350
Right so back to Filip.

00:26:00.350 --> 00:26:04.030
So.

00:26:04.030 --> 00:26:05.210
A workflow.

00:26:05.210 --> 00:26:08.110
And shiny fluent
and shiny react are

00:26:08.110 --> 00:26:11.500
going to be fully
open source, and we

00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:15.100
are excited to share our
frameworks and our way of work,

00:26:15.100 --> 00:26:19.480
but we think that sometimes
frameworks are just not enough.

00:26:19.480 --> 00:26:23.560
They don't cut it on their own.

00:26:23.560 --> 00:26:27.250
And this is why we want
to create another resource

00:26:27.250 --> 00:26:29.050
for our community.

00:26:32.620 --> 00:26:35.350
So in other
communities, if you

00:26:35.350 --> 00:26:37.570
want to create your
WordPress page,

00:26:37.570 --> 00:26:40.000
if you want to create
your e-commerce store,

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:43.630
if you want to create your
study bootstrap website,

00:26:43.630 --> 00:26:46.400
you can gross,

00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:50.780
I bet, thousands, maybe
hundreds, depending

00:26:50.780 --> 00:26:55.410
on the use case, premade
quality templates and layouts.

00:26:55.410 --> 00:27:00.770
You can choose, pick the one you
like, you can download or buy

00:27:00.770 --> 00:27:06.230
and customize with a fraction
of work necessary to build

00:27:06.230 --> 00:27:08.960
everything from scratch.

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.210
And this is why we

00:27:14.270 --> 00:27:20.740
we decided to do the same
thing for the R and Shiny community.

00:27:20.740 --> 00:27:32.740
So, we decided to
share some of our work,

00:27:32.740 --> 00:27:40.750
and our Shiny apps are often
complimented for how they look

00:27:40.750 --> 00:27:46.180
and we are quite proud about
taking care of a great design.

00:27:46.180 --> 00:27:51.850
We deeply care here about
apps being both easy to use

00:27:51.850 --> 00:27:55.360
and beautiful and useful.

00:27:55.360 --> 00:28:00.460
So some of the layouts that
were crafted by our engineers

00:28:00.460 --> 00:28:03.520
and designers are
going to be available,

00:28:03.520 --> 00:28:08.080
some of them for free, some
of them to buy on the platform

00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:11.440
that we are going to
share with everyone.

00:28:14.920 --> 00:28:19.600
So what did we promise today?

00:28:19.600 --> 00:28:23.290
First, shiny fluent
and shiny react

00:28:23.290 --> 00:28:26.800
are going to be
open source, you can

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:32.350
create great enterprise, great
applications especially

00:28:32.350 --> 00:28:35.050
for enterprise ecosystems
with shiny fluent,

00:28:35.050 --> 00:28:40.940
and we should expect
more React

00:28:40.940 --> 00:28:43.280
libraries is being
part of it, as R

00:28:43.280 --> 00:28:46.450
packages available to us.

00:28:46.450 --> 00:28:52.220
Second, we will open source
a lot of our internal tools

00:28:52.220 --> 00:28:55.790
to empower the whole
community and to leverage

00:28:55.790 --> 00:28:59.400
what we've discovered
in many of our projects.

00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:04.370
So that the whole community
can move forward much faster.

00:29:04.370 --> 00:29:06.410
At least we hope so.

00:29:06.410 --> 00:29:10.950
Third, we will help kick start

00:29:10.950 --> 00:29:13.880
hopefully more teams and
more Shiny developers,

00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:19.820
that want to work with
premade templates and layouts.

00:29:19.820 --> 00:29:24.590
All this, we do because we
want to empower data scientists

00:29:24.590 --> 00:29:29.180
and scientists and researchers
worldwide to create

00:29:29.180 --> 00:29:31.560
more and better Shiny apps.

00:29:31.560 --> 00:29:33.890
So that together, we
can have more impact

00:29:33.890 --> 00:29:38.680
and help other people make
wiser decisions with the data.

